  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><strong>Aura</strong> faint (+1), moderate (+2/+3), or strong (+4/+5) Alteration and Enhancement; <strong>CL</strong> 3rd (+1), 6th (+2), 9th (+3), 12th (+4), or 15th (+5)<br>\n<strong>Slot</strong> neck; <strong>Price</strong> 3,500 gp (+1), 14,000 gp (+2), 31,500 gp (+3), 56,000 gp (+4), or 87,500 gp (+5); <strong>Weight</strong> 1&nbsp;lb.</p>\n<p>Frequently worn by specialist fighters, these wood and leather talismans are worn around the neck. While worn, they provide a competence bonus to one combat maneuver (chosen when the item is created) and an equal enhancement bonus to natural armor.</p>\n<p><strong>Construction Requirements</strong><br>\nForge Charm, Alteration sphere, Enhancement sphere; <strong>Cost</strong> 1,750 gp (+1), 7,000 gp (+2), 15,750 gp (+3), 28,000 gp (+4), or 43,750 gp (+5)</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/charms#toc45\">Source: Spheres of Power Wiki</a></p>",
      "instructions": "<p>Reviewed selection: base +1; one crafted combat maneuver not selected.</p><p>The wood-and-leather talisman grants +1 enhancement to natural armor plus +1 competence to one crafted maneuver. The maneuver remains unselected and conditional; no global CMB bonus or CMD bonus is granted. In particular, do not inherit the Gauntlet of Maneuvers' separate defensive bonus. The natural-armor enhancement is distinct from a base natural armor bonus.</p>",
      "unidentified": ""
    },
